### Health check - confirm server is running
GET http://localhost:3000/ HTTP/1.1

###

### Get all universities
GET http://localhost:3000/university HTTP/1.1

###

### Get one university with departments and professors (replace with a real id from your seed output)
GET http://localhost:3000/university/cmst7l9sk0000no1huhk6rdaz HTTP/1.1

###

### Get one university - not found
GET http://localhost:3000/university/doesnotexist HTTP/1.1

###

### Get all professors
GET http://localhost:3000/professors HTTP/1.1

###

### Get one professor with department, courses, and reviews (replace with a real id)
GET http://localhost:3000/professors/cmst7la06000bno1hvkq38wy2 HTTP/1.1

###

### Get one professor - not found
GET http://localhost:3000/professors/doesnotexist HTTP/1.1

###

### Get all courses
GET http://localhost:3000/courses HTTP/1.1

###

### Get one course with professors and reviews (replace with a real id)
GET http://localhost:3000/courses/cmst7l9yt0005no1hxn7ga5ov HTTP/1.1

###

### Get one course - not found
GET http://localhost:3000/courses/doesnotexist HTTP/1.1



### Sign up a new user
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signup HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "newstudent4@example.com",
    "password": "mypassword123"
}

###

### Sign up - duplicate email (should fail with 409)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signup HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "newstudent3@example.com",
    "password": "mypassword123"
}

###

### Log in with a seeded test user (from seed.ts: password123)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "newstudent4@example.com",
    "password": "mypassword123"
}

###

### Log in - wrong password (should fail with 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "teststudent1@example.com",
    "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###

### Log in - email that doesn't exist (should fail with 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "doesnotexist@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}


### Create a review - NO TOKEN (should fail with 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/reviews HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "professorId": "REPLACE_WITH_PROFESSOR_ID",
    "courseId": "REPLACE_WITH_COURSE_ID",
    "qualityRating": 5,
    "difficultyRating": 3,
    "wouldTakeAgain": true,
    "gradeReceived": "A",
    "comment": "Great professor, explains things clearly."
}

###

### Create a review - WITH TOKEN (paste the token from your login response above)
POST http://localhost:3000/reviews HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN

{
    "professorId": "REPLACE_WITH_PROFESSOR_ID",
    "courseId": "REPLACE_WITH_COURSE_ID",
    "qualityRating": 5,
    "difficultyRating": 3,
    "wouldTakeAgain": true,
    "gradeReceived": "A",
    "comment": "Great professor, explains things clearly."
}

